791     {\cf20 // Tables}\par
792     {\cf20 // - Full-featured replacement for old Columns API.}\par
793     {\cf20 // - See Demo->Tables for demo code. See top of imgui_tables.cpp for general commentary.}\par
794     {\cf20 // - See ImGuiTableFlags_ and ImGuiTableColumnFlags_ enums for a description of available flags.}\par
795     {\cf20 // The typical call flow is:}\par
796     {\cf20 // - 1. Call BeginTable(), early out if returning false.}\par
797     {\cf20 // - 2. Optionally call TableSetupColumn() to submit column name/flags/defaults.}\par
798     {\cf20 // - 3. Optionally call TableSetupScrollFreeze() to request scroll freezing of columns/rows.}\par
799     {\cf20 // - 4. Optionally call TableHeadersRow() to submit a header row. Names are pulled from TableSetupColumn() data.}\par
800     {\cf20 // - 5. Populate contents:}\par
801     {\cf20 //    - In most situations you can use TableNextRow() + TableSetColumnIndex(N) to start appending into a column.}\par
802     {\cf20 //    - If you are using tables as a sort of grid, where every column is holding the same type of contents,}\par
803     {\cf20 //      you may prefer using TableNextColumn() instead of TableNextRow() + TableSetColumnIndex().}\par
804     {\cf20 //      TableNextColumn() will automatically wrap-around into the next row if needed.}\par
805     {\cf20 //    - IMPORTANT: Comparatively to the old Columns() API, we need to call TableNextColumn() for the first column!}\par
806     {\cf20 //    - Summary of possible call flow:}\par
807     {\cf20 //        - TableNextRow() -> TableSetColumnIndex(0) -> Text("Hello 0") -> TableSetColumnIndex(1) -> Text("Hello 1")  // OK}\par
808     {\cf20 //        - TableNextRow() -> TableNextColumn()      -> Text("Hello 0") -> TableNextColumn()      -> Text("Hello 1")  // OK}\par
809     {\cf20 //        -                   TableNextColumn()      -> Text("Hello 0") -> TableNextColumn()      -> Text("Hello 1")  // OK: TableNextColumn() automatically gets to next row!}\par
810     {\cf20 //        - TableNextRow()                           -> Text("Hello 0")                                               // Not OK! Missing TableSetColumnIndex() or TableNextColumn()! Text will not appear!}\par
811     {\cf20 // - 5. Call EndTable()}\par
