995     {\cf20 // Inputs Utilities: Shortcut Testing & Routing [BETA]}\par
996     {\cf20 // - ImGuiKeyChord = a ImGuiKey + optional ImGuiMod_Alt/ImGuiMod_Ctrl/ImGuiMod_Shift/ImGuiMod_Super.}\par
997     {\cf20 //       ImGuiKey_C                          // Accepted by functions taking ImGuiKey or ImGuiKeyChord arguments)}\par
998     {\cf20 //       ImGuiMod_Ctrl | ImGuiKey_C          // Accepted by functions taking ImGuiKeyChord arguments)}\par
999     {\cf20 //   only ImGuiMod_XXX values are legal to combine with an ImGuiKey. You CANNOT combine two ImGuiKey values.}\par
1000     {\cf20 // - The general idea is that several callers may register interest in a shortcut, and only one owner gets it.}\par
1001     {\cf20 //      Parent   -> call Shortcut(Ctrl+S)    // When Parent is focused, Parent gets the shortcut.}\par
1002     {\cf20 //        Child1 -> call Shortcut(Ctrl+S)    // When Child1 is focused, Child1 gets the shortcut (Child1 overrides Parent shortcuts)}\par
1003     {\cf20 //        Child2 -> no call                  // When Child2 is focused, Parent gets the shortcut.}\par
1004     {\cf20 //   The whole system is order independent, so if Child1 makes its calls before Parent, results will be identical.}\par
1005     {\cf20 //   This is an important property as it facilitate working with foreign code or larger codebase.}\par
1006     {\cf20 // - To understand the difference:}\par
1007     {\cf20 //   - IsKeyChordPressed() compares mods and call IsKeyPressed() -> function has no side-effect.}\par
1008     {\cf20 //   - Shortcut() submits a route, routes are resolved, if it currently can be routed it calls IsKeyChordPressed() -> function has (desirable) side-effects as it can prevents another call from getting the route.}\par
1009     {\cf20 // - Visualize registered routes in 'Metrics/Debugger->Inputs'.}\par
1010     IMGUI_API {\cf18 bool}          Shortcut(ImGuiKeyChord key_chord, ImGuiInputFlags flags = 0);\par
1011     IMGUI_API {\cf18 void}          SetNextItemShortcut(ImGuiKeyChord key_chord, ImGuiInputFlags flags = 0);\par
