1136 {\cf20 // Flags for ImGui::BeginChild()}\par
1137 {\cf20 // (Legacy: bit 0 must always correspond to ImGuiChildFlags_Border to be backward compatible with old API using 'bool border = false'.}\par
1138 {\cf20 // About using AutoResizeX/AutoResizeY flags:}\par
1139 {\cf20 // - May be combined with SetNextWindowSizeConstraints() to set a min/max size for each axis (see "Demo->Child->Auto-resize with Constraints").}\par
1140 {\cf20 // - Size measurement for a given axis is only performed when the child window is within visible boundaries, or is just appearing.}\par
1141 {\cf20 //   - This allows BeginChild() to return false when not within boundaries (e.g. when scrolling), which is more optimal. BUT it won't update its auto-size while clipped.}\par
1142 {\cf20 //     While not perfect, it is a better default behavior as the always-on performance gain is more valuable than the occasional "resizing after becoming visible again" glitch.}\par
1143 {\cf20 //   - You may also use ImGuiChildFlags_AlwaysAutoResize to force an update even when child window is not in view.}\par
1144 {\cf20 //     HOWEVER PLEASE UNDERSTAND THAT DOING SO WILL PREVENT BeginChild() FROM EVER RETURNING FALSE, disabling benefits of coarse clipping.}\par
