1569     {\cf20 // Keyboard Modifiers (explicitly submitted by backend via AddKeyEvent() calls)}\par
1570     {\cf20 // - This is mirroring the data also written to io.KeyCtrl, io.KeyShift, io.KeyAlt, io.KeySuper, in a format allowing}\par
1571     {\cf20 //   them to be accessed via standard key API, allowing calls such as IsKeyPressed(), IsKeyReleased(), querying duration etc.}\par
1572     {\cf20 // - Code polling every key (e.g. an interface to detect a key press for input mapping) might want to ignore those}\par
1573     {\cf20 //   and prefer using the real keys (e.g. ImGuiKey_LeftCtrl, ImGuiKey_RightCtrl instead of ImGuiMod_Ctrl).}\par
1574     {\cf20 // - In theory the value of keyboard modifiers should be roughly equivalent to a logical or of the equivalent left/right keys.}\par
1575     {\cf20 //   In practice: it's complicated; mods are often provided from different sources. Keyboard layout, IME, sticky keys and}\par
1576     {\cf20 //   backends tend to interfere and break that equivalence. The safer decision is to relay that ambiguity down to the end-user...}\par
1577     {\cf20 // - On macOS, we swap Cmd(Super) and Ctrl keys at the time of the io.AddKeyEvent() call.}\par
1578     ImGuiMod_None                   = 0,\par
1579     ImGuiMod_Ctrl                   = 1 << 12, {\cf20 // Ctrl (non-macOS), Cmd (macOS)}\par
1580     ImGuiMod_Shift                  = 1 << 13, {\cf20 // Shift}\par
1581     ImGuiMod_Alt                    = 1 << 14, {\cf20 // Option/Menu}\par
1582     ImGuiMod_Super                  = 1 << 15, {\cf20 // Windows/Super (non-macOS), Ctrl (macOS)}\par
1583     ImGuiMod_Mask_                  = 0xF000,  {\cf20 // 4-bits}\par
