2680 {\cf20 // Helper: Key->Value storage}\par
2681 {\cf20 // Typically you don't have to worry about this since a storage is held within each Window.}\par
2682 {\cf20 // We use it to e.g. store collapse state for a tree (Int 0/1)}\par
2683 {\cf20 // This is optimized for efficient lookup (dichotomy into a contiguous buffer) and rare insertion (typically tied to user interactions aka max once a frame)}\par
2684 {\cf20 // You can use it as custom user storage for temporary values. Declare your own storage if, for example:}\par
2685 {\cf20 // - You want to manipulate the open/close state of a particular sub-tree in your interface (tree node uses Int 0/1 to store their state).}\par
2686 {\cf20 // - You want to store custom debug data easily without adding or editing structures in your code (probably not efficient, but convenient)}\par
2687 {\cf20 // Types are NOT stored, so it is up to you to make sure your Key don't collide with different types.}\par
