3023 {\cf20 // Special Draw callback value to request renderer backend to reset the graphics/render state.}\par
3024 {\cf20 // The renderer backend needs to handle this special value, otherwise it will crash trying to call a function at this address.}\par
3025 {\cf20 // This is useful, for example, if you submitted callbacks which you know have altered the render state and you want it to be restored.}\par
3026 {\cf20 // Render state is not reset by default because they are many perfectly useful way of altering render state (e.g. changing shader/blending settings before an Image call).}\par
3027 {\cf21 #define ImDrawCallback_ResetRenderState     (ImDrawCallback)(-8)}\par
