3172     {\cf20 // Primitives}\par
3173     {\cf20 // - Filled shapes must always use clockwise winding order. The anti-aliasing fringe depends on it. Counter-clockwise shapes will have "inward" anti-aliasing.}\par
3174     {\cf20 // - For rectangular primitives, "p_min" and "p_max" represent the upper-left and lower-right corners.}\par
3175     {\cf20 // - For circle primitives, use "num_segments == 0" to automatically calculate tessellation (preferred).}\par
3176     {\cf20 //   In older versions (until Dear ImGui 1.77) the AddCircle functions defaulted to num_segments == 12.}\par
3177     {\cf20 //   In future versions we will use textures to provide cheaper and higher-quality circles.}\par
3178     {\cf20 //   Use AddNgon() and AddNgonFilled() functions if you need to guarantee a specific number of sides.}\par
