3381 {\cf20 // Load and rasterize multiple TTF/OTF fonts into a same texture. The font atlas will build a single texture holding:}\par
3382 {\cf20 //  - One or more fonts.}\par
3383 {\cf20 //  - Custom graphics data needed to render the shapes needed by Dear ImGui.}\par
3384 {\cf20 //  - Mouse cursor shapes for software cursor rendering (unless setting 'Flags |= ImFontAtlasFlags_NoMouseCursors' in the font atlas).}\par
3385 {\cf20 // It is the user-code responsibility to setup/build the atlas, then upload the pixel data into a texture accessible by your graphics api.}\par
3386 {\cf20 //  - Optionally, call any of the AddFont*** functions. If you don't call any, the default font embedded in the code will be loaded for you.}\par
3387 {\cf20 //  - Call GetTexDataAsAlpha8() or GetTexDataAsRGBA32() to build and retrieve pixels data.}\par
3388 {\cf20 //  - Upload the pixels data into a texture within your graphics system (see imgui_impl_xxxx.cpp examples)}\par
3389 {\cf20 //  - Call SetTexID(my_tex_id); and pass the pointer/identifier to your texture in a format natural to your graphics API.}\par
3390 {\cf20 //    This value will be passed back to you during rendering to identify the texture. Read FAQ entry about ImTextureID for more details.}\par
3391 {\cf20 // Common pitfalls:}\par
3392 {\cf20 // - If you pass a 'glyph_ranges' array to AddFont*** functions, you need to make sure that your array persist up until the}\par
3393 {\cf20 //   atlas is build (when calling GetTexData*** or Build()). We only copy the pointer, not the data.}\par
3394 {\cf20 // - Important: By default, AddFontFromMemoryTTF() takes ownership of the data. Even though we are not writing to it, we will free the pointer on destruction.}\par
3395 {\cf20 //   You can set font_cfg->FontDataOwnedByAtlas=false to keep ownership of your data and it won't be freed,}\par
3396 {\cf20 // - Even though many functions are suffixed with "TTF", OTF data is supported just as well.}\par
3397 {\cf20 // - This is an old API and it is currently awkward for those and various other reasons! We will address them in the future!}\par
3398 {\cf17 struct }ImFontAtlas\par
